:: day1_npc_marta_tray [nobr]
<<npcPortrait "marta" "Marta">>
<h3>A Meal Tray   From Marta</h3>

<p>A tray appears at my door. Not brought by a servant   just there, set on the floor outside, when I open the door after Ash leaves. A palace kitchen tray, covered with a clean cloth.</p>

<p>Under the cloth: soup (thick, onion and thyme, the same recipe Marta has been making since I was nine). Bread (warm, fresh, the good kind). Two cheese pastries (golden, rosemary). An apple pastry (cinnamon, sugar, the childhood recipe) and a folded note.</p>

<p><em>Eat everything. You're thin.<br>
Same stool. Same pastries. Same Marta.<br>
  M.</em></p>

<p>She's not allowed in the tower. The Silverveil restrict access during post-ritual recovery. So she sent a tray. Through channels   probably Alva arranged the logistics, probably Brin carried it to the bridge, probably a Silverveil apprentice brought it the rest of the way.</p>

<p>The food is perfect. It tastes the same. Everything Marta makes tastes the same regardless of the body eating it, because Marta's cooking transcends the merely physical and operates on the level of the soul.</p>

<p>I eat everything. I'm still hungry afterward, because Vael was right about the metabolism. But the hunger is manageable and the soup is warm in my stomach and the note is under my pillow beside the Queen's letter and for the first time today I feel something that is not horror or grief or clinical detachment.</p>

<p>I feel fed. Which is Marta's magic, and it is the most powerful magic in this tower.</p>

<<set $d1f_npc_marta_tray to true>>
<<set $energy += 15>>
<<set $stress -= 8>>
<<set $repStaff += 1>>

<div class="scene-end">
  [[Continue → |day1_door_hub]]
</div>
